[ ] Unwind projection from the live file (file is all-materialized) =occurrence-surface $REVERSAL of the shipped atomic lane (README 2026-07-26 cont.2). LANDED 2026-07-28: removed extend_with_projected_occurrences from From<Workspace> + both CLI read collectors, and the plumbing that only fed the union (Projection struct, load_domain_model_with_projection, without_occurrences, load_model_materialized). load_domain_model is materialized-only now; a recurring plan surfaces ONE materialized present token on read, no projected window (e2e-proven). The engine (render_occurrences/render_occurrence/next_active_slot, deviation read/write, frame fix) SURVIVES for the write-path stamper + the future calendar view. REMAINING: the re-home child below.$ !2 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[ ] Re-home projection to future (calendar) and past (analytics) $Projection survives only as a query concern, never a core data-model piece. Future occurrences render in a read-only calendar view; past completions surface as analytics over archive/. HARD RULE: projection must never feed an index-shape query (results resolving to file:line:col to jump to/edit) — a projected occurrence has no line, so it would break the qflist as a first-class EDITING surface. The .actions file stays all-materialized; the nvim virtual-line gymnastics are obviated because present occurrences are real lines.$ !3 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
    >[x] Seal the projection to sync leak $Sync reconciles owned artifacts only; a projected occurrence has no standalone resource to reconcile and no line for apply_sync to locate. sync_calendar now loads a window-0 model (Projection::without_occurrences / ctx.load_model_materialized) so occurrences are structurally absent from plan_sync, not filtered by a fragile flag. Regression-locked in workspace_store.rs. Relates to the two-assembly-sites debt in =occurrence-view.$ #019f9bdf-bad8-7940-a77e-98be6bf8b04e
    >[x] Re-cohere graphd with the materialized model $DONE 2026-07-28. Getting-it-working: removed the dead per-action external_schedule_id projection (RDF insert.rs + JSON-LD jsonld.rs) and stripped it from actions.schema/context/example v4; kept hasExternalScheduleId on the Plan node (the VTODO UID, still valid). Taking-advantage: graphd already projects plan_id->cco:prescribed_by + external_occurrence_key, but post-unwind materialized tokens reached it with plan_id=None; core loader hydration (see lineage item) restores the live link, so graphd expresses the prescription edge with ZERO new graphd code. e2e-proven via the real graphd binary (query raw: token -> prescribed_by -> plan). graphd is a pure DomainModel projector — no sync-store/archive access of its own; the edge must arrive in the model.$ #019fa7a6-600f-7221-a7aa-7b858097fa48
[ ] Build the present-stamping lane (atomic and templated) =stamping-lane ~ $LANDED 2026-07-28 (atomic + templated both e2e-proven; the stamp-present child is completed & in the archive). REMAINING here: only the archived-lineage child below. DESIGN (kept for reference): the single materialized lane — the two-lane split (project atomic / stamp templated) collapses (README 2026-07-26 cont.2). On the write path a generator stamps the PRESENT due occurrence: atomic = a synthesized childless root from the master VTODO (SUMMARY->title, CATEGORIES->contexts, PRIORITY->priority, id = occurrence UUIDv5 = hash(plan UID, slot)); templated = the same root + the template step-forest grafted beneath it via parent_override in instantiate_template (graft_template_steps in reconcile.rs). Also sealed the materialized-token sync leak: plan_sync excludes occurrence tokens + their grafted subtrees (occurrence_subtree_ids). GUARDRAIL held: never materialize the future — one occurrence per plan; the next is generated on completion, RRULE read fresh.$ !2 +caldav #019fa019-079f-7681-bb22-d64ab1a9f78c
    >[ ] Snapshot plan-lineage onto the archived instance at completion $The ARCHIVED half of occurrence lineage. The LIVE half LANDED 2026-07-28: the loader (hydrate_occurrence_links) restamps plan_id + external_occurrence_key onto materialized tokens from the sync store, so graphd projects cco:prescribed_by while an occurrence is live. THIS item: at crystallization (completion/archival) snapshot the SEMANTIC edge onto the archived instance — realizes plan-M at temporal position T + a human label — so it survives the plan being edited/deleted (invoice-snapshots-price-at-sale). Do NOT reverse-derive from the current RRULE. Snapshot the semantic edge, never the occurrence-id hash. End state: graphd projects coherent history over live (hydrated) + archived (snapshotted) facts.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-3dd0-7993-bcae-c0abfbf8f60d
[ ] Add a delete verb, distinct from close/cancel $Consequence of the fact-model: there is no immutability invariant (unenforceable across hand-editable plaintext + foreign CalDAV clients + eventually-consistent sync, so declaring it would be a lie). close/cancel are STATE TRANSITIONS (the fact persists, status changes); delete is RETRACTION FROM HISTORY (erase the thing). The user declares intent via the verb; the system does not infer human-vs-machine provenance. Safe because graphd degrades gracefully over a tolerant world (dangling refs / missing nodes / partial reads) — a deleted fact is a hole a projection absorbs. History-preserving stays the default by convention; delete is the deliberate, higher-friction exception. NOTE: likely a general workspace/action-lifecycle verb, not caldav-specific — may belong in a core charter; seeded here because the fact-model that motivates it is documented in this README.$ !3 +caldav #019fa019-5d05-7ee0-a09a-b4e20c2a304a
